preConditionHook:
// The magnetic middle: a breakout attempt inside a trading range gets pulled
// back to the range's midpoint, so take profit there. The window is the N bars
// ENDING ONE BAR AGO, so the target level does not move with the bar that
// reaches it.
//
// TICK UNITS: the merged pseudocode placed the target toleranceTicks x tickSize
// short of the midpoint. A tick cannot be converted to price without MinMove /
// PriceScale, neither of which is registered in EL_FEATURES, so the tolerance
// is a FRACTION OF THE RANGE HEIGHT instead -- portable across instruments and
// free, since both extremes are already computed here. At the 0.01 default the
// band is 1% of the range's own height.
//
// EL: highest(high, rangeLookback)[1] -- lowercase, as the feature register
// writes it -- is the previous bar's highest, the N bars ending one bar ago,
// i.e. today's high[1..rangeLookback]. It bottoms out in Extremes(), EL SOURCE: seeded at the first bar of its window, scanning
// the rest with a strict, tolerance-carrying comparison (see Breakout), so this
// seeds at high[1] and scans high[2..rangeLookback] with el_gt/el_lt --
// CloseAbovePriorHighestHigh is the reference for the offset window.
priorRangeHigh = high[1];
priorRangeLow = low[1];
for (int i = 2; i <= (int)rangeLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], priorRangeHigh)) priorRangeHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], priorRangeLow)) priorRangeLow = low[i];
}
targetMid = (priorRangeHigh + priorRangeLow) / 2;
targetBand = toleranceFraction * (priorRangeHigh - priorRangeLow);
